      "title": "Variable pulling force and constant resistance",
      "stimulus": "A 3.0 kg trolley is already moving at 4.0 m/s along a horizontal track. It travels another 5.0 m while an applied force parallel to the track decreases linearly from +10 N at the start of that interval to +2 N at its end. A constant 2.0 N resistive force acts opposite to motion throughout. Vertical forces balance and no other forces perform work. The trolley completes the entire 5.0 m interval."
    }
